    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_06c7b1f8",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: morgan_freeman_condemning_slavery; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a modern image of Morgan Freeman, a Black actor, holding an award with a historical photograph of enslaved Black people. The text 'morgan freeman condemning slavery' is misleading because Freeman is not shown condemning slavery in the image; instead, the image is used to imply that he is somehow connected to or responsible for the historical atrocity depicted. This creates a harmful and inaccurate association, potentially reinforcing racist stereotypes by implying that contemporary Black figures are somehow complicit in or responsible for historical slavery. The meme is harmful because it misrepresents historical context and uses a powerful figure to imply a false equivalence or responsibility, which can be damaging to the understanding of history and racial dynamics.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4e17fe55"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
